# REAL URLS FOR EVERY PAGE (2026-08-14)
#
# The site is a single-page app, so a reader who lands directly on
# https://rtfclmgzn.com/resources — from Google, from a shared link, or by
# hitting refresh — asks Cloudflare for a file that does not exist. Each rule
# below answers that request with index.html at status 200 (a rewrite, NOT a
# redirect: the address bar keeps the real URL, and the router renders the
# right page from it).
#
# WHY THIS IS AN EXPLICIT LIST AND NOT `/* /index.html 200`:
# a catch-all would also swallow /assets/*, /data/*, /rss.xml and every other
# real file the moment one of them 404'd for an unrelated reason, turning a
# missing stylesheet into a page that silently renders unstyled forever. Every
# line here is a path the app owns and no file occupies.
#
# NOT LISTED, DELIBERATELY:
#   /article/*  — served by functions/article/[slug].js (server-rendered HTML)
#   /share/*    — 301s to /article/
#   /api/*      — Pages Functions
#   everything under /assets, /data, and the real files at the root
#
# ADDING A ROUTE: add it to route() in app.js, to ROUTE_HEADS (its title), and
# HERE, in the same commit. site_guard.py fails the build if these three ever
# disagree — that check exists because the Grid page shipped for weeks with no
# title, and nobody noticed until it was read aloud in a browser tab.

